@@ -11,3 +11,8 @@ sidebar_position: 7
 |---------------------|------|-------|---------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|
 | `target_duty_cycle` |      | float | 0.0     | Fixed duty cycle fraction (0–1 of pwmMaxDriver); if > 0 enters manual PWM mode with hard-fixed duty (no PD control, no MPPT tracking) |
 | `sweep_speed`       |      | float | 4.0     | Global-sweep speed; scales both per-tick cap and limit-tracking gain (clamp ≥ 0.1) |
+| `rev_k`             |      | float | 2.5     | P&O reversal threshold in noise units: a power change counts once it exceeds `rev_k`·√(2·var), with var the noise variance of one decision-period mean. It is derived from second differences of `period_min_ms` means, corrected for the power filter's correlation (clamp ≥ 0). Until 8 noise samples exist the fixed threshold applies |
+| `period_min_ms`     | ms   | float | 33      | Shortest P&O decision period; the tracker returns to it on a new MPP record, a limiter hand-back, a cloud-recovery reversal or 45 s without a reversal (clamp ≥ 5) |
+| `period_max_ms`     | ms   | float | 500     | Longest P&O decision period (clamp ≥ `period_min_ms`). The perturbation slew scales with `period_min_ms`/period |
+| `period_grow`       |      | float | 1.3     | Factor applied to the decision period on each reversal without a new MPP record (clamp ≥ 1) |
+| `rev_floor_w`       | W    | float | 0.05    | Lowest P&O reversal threshold (clamp ≥ 0.001) |
